WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:06.640
The thin, pale humanoid anomaly had just found
itself… in Minecraft, of all places.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:11.759
The all too familiar wail of emergency alarms
rang out through the corridors of the Foundation

00:00:11.759 --> 00:00:12.799
facility.

00:00:12.799 --> 00:00:16.170
It had happened again, another containment
breach.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:20.470
Of course, the on-site personnel were more
than familiar with the protocols for a situation

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:26.160
like this, so well-versed in what to do during
an emergency that it had become second nature.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:30.410
Whether they were research staff evacuating
for their own safety, or security teams moving

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:35.090
in to recapture the escaped anomaly and get
the situation under control, everyone was

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:39.230
moving like they had been programmed, muscle
memory taking over.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:45.330
The loose anomaly was none other than SCP-096,
all Foundation personnel were alerted and

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:48.289
reminded not to look directly at the creature.

00:00:48.289 --> 00:00:52.859
There was just one problem: they couldn’t
look even if they’d ignored their order

00:00:52.859 --> 00:00:54.100
to try.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:57.910
Nobody could… because the Shy Guy was nowhere
to be found.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:00.660
Well, nowhere in the real world, at least.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:04.739
This whole situation – bizarre even by the
Foundation’s standards – had all started

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:09.259
with an experiment involving a member of the
disposable D Class Personnel.

00:01:09.259 --> 00:01:14.210
Yet another dangerous convict severing one
of several life sentences, now being used

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:19.650
as an expendable human lab rat for the Foundation’s
often sinister purposes.

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:24.450
The experiment in question was an attempt
to further test the limitations of SCP-096’s

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:25.450
abilities.

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:31.080
By now, the Foundation had done extensive
research into the creature known as the Shy

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:32.080
Guy.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:36.310
They knew its particular brand of anomalous
qualities were triggered when anyone looked

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:38.110
directly at it.

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:44.400
Being observed would instantaneously send
SCP-096 into an uncontrollable rage state,

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:48.650
causing it to pursue its observer until they
were no longer standing.

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:54.189
SCP-096 was known to be able to travel at
speeds so relentless it was pretty much possible

00:01:54.189 --> 00:01:55.390
to stop.

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:59.970
One moment it was sobbing and screeching in
its cell having just been observed, and minutes

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:05.880
later, the wide-jawed, long-limbed monster
was standing behind whoever had seen it, making

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:10.100
its screaming face the image its victim took
to the grave with them.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:15.010
Foundation researchers knew that SCP-096’s
rage state could be triggered by as little

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:18.500
as someone seeing the slightest hint of a
creature.

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:22.890
Even if the Shy Guy had been captured as a
tiny speck in the background of a photograph,

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:27.350
it would come after anyone whose eyes so much
as glanced over that speck.

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:34.240
It also didn’t matter how far away the observer
was – SCP-096 couldn’t be outrun, it could

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.860
track down anyone wherever they were in the
world.

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:41.790
But what if a person who had observed the
Shy Guy was no longer in the world…

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:46.450
The experiment had taken a lot of trial and
error – after all, digitizing a human being

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:50.519
and transforming their entire consciousness
into code was no easy task.

00:02:50.519 --> 00:02:55.210
But the Foundation wasn’t above breaking
more than a few eggs to make an omelette,

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:58.980
especially when those eggs were the brains
of a few D Class Personnel.

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:04.540
Actually, the first test subjects turned out
more scrambled or fried, certainly overdone,

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:07.170
given the amount of smoke coming from their
ears.

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:11.950
But eventually, the research team had perfected
the device they had dubbed the ‘Neural Harness’,

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:16.740
a headset that could translate a person’s
mind into pure digital code.

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:20.890
Their consciousness would be extracted from
their body, leaving their physical form an

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:25.849
empty shell while a digital copy of them was
able to traverse the local on-site computer

00:03:25.849 --> 00:03:26.849
network.

00:03:26.849 --> 00:03:30.989
Of course, the Foundation wasn’t about to
let a digitized D Class run amok with their

00:03:30.989 --> 00:03:36.230
systems, so their coding experts wrote a number
of specialized parameters into their successful

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:37.230
test subject.

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:42.170
Now, the digital D Class could be programmed
to follow the Foundation’s directive.

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:46.959
From his perspective, it was like he was floating
through cyberspace, towards the system the

00:03:46.959 --> 00:03:53.490
Foundation had directed him too: a surveillance
camera inside SCP-096’s cell that usually

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:55.180
remained inactive.

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:56.420
But not today.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:04:00.939
The camera blinked to life as soon as the
D Class’s code-based consciousness reached

00:04:00.939 --> 00:04:06.659
it, and through it, he was able to observe
SCP-096, sitting against the far wall of its

00:04:06.659 --> 00:04:10.829
containment chamber, gently whimpering and
rocking back and forth.

00:04:10.829 --> 00:04:16.290
That is, until the creature felt that familiar
sensation of being watched.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:21.880
It stood up, enraged, wailing uncontrollably
as the D Class watched from within the camera.

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:27.410
Then, a split second later, SCP-096 appeared
to blink out of existence.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:32.630
It hadn’t worked, the experiment had failed,
and the digital D Class began to panic.

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:36.380
Before the Foundation’s coders could stop
him, he frantically scoured the local network

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:40.580
for anything, some kind of escape route back
into the real world.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:44.560
Maybe, he thought, if he could get back into
his body, it wouldn’t count?

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:48.990
Technically, his digital self was separate
from his physical form, so he might get out

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:52.720
of SCP-096’s clutches on a technicality.

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:57.330
But it was impossible, his body was already
burned out by the Neural Harness, there was

00:04:57.330 --> 00:05:00.259
no way for the D Class to transfer himself
back.

00:05:00.259 --> 00:05:02.840
There was only one option left: hide.

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:07.889
And, as it turned out, someone had forgotten
to uninstall a certain building game from

00:05:07.889 --> 00:05:11.169
a computer in one of the Foundation doctor’s
offices.

00:05:11.169 --> 00:05:15.940
The D Class’s digitized mind zapped him
into Minecraft; from his point of view, it

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:18.360
was just like he existed within the game itself.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:23.220
He did a computerized equivalent of breathing
a sigh of relief, only to take back all those

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:28.660
ones and zeros in a horrified gasp as he noticed
a tall, wiry-framed figure before him.

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:35.090
It hadn’t worked, SCP-096 had still managed
to follow him into Minecraft.

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:39.300
Even in a world of computer code, the Shy
Guy was able to dispatch its digital observer

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:44.780
quite easily, and what had once been a living
human mind in the form of binary code was

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:45.919
quickly deleted.

00:05:45.919 --> 00:05:50.540
But that’s when SCP-096 started to take
notice of its surroundings.

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:54.950
With the most recent person to see it gone,
it had a chance to actually take in where

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:56.060
it was.

00:05:56.060 --> 00:06:00.830
The bright rays of warm light coming down
from a cube-shaped sun reveal a welcoming

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:05.380
landscape all around, constructed entirely
from cubes.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:11.630
It fascinated SCP-096, instilling a kind of
childlike wonder in the Shy Guy the likes

00:06:11.630 --> 00:06:13.960
of which it hadn’t experienced since…

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:16.169
well, since it couldn’t remember when.

00:06:16.169 --> 00:06:21.760
Rather than leaving, instantly reappearing
in its containment chamber, SCP-096 made the

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:24.690
conscious decision to start exploring.

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:29.850
There was a mountainous biome surrounding
SCP-096, stony spires reaching up towards

00:06:29.850 --> 00:06:34.460
a clear sky, with a waterfall cascading its
way down the nearest of them.

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:38.470
At the foot of one of the mountains was the
opening to a cave, which the Shy Guy found

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:40.099
itself wandering towards.

00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:44.199
The light from the sun, while a pleasant and
welcome change to the surroundings it was

00:06:44.199 --> 00:06:48.479
used to, was a little harsh on SCP-096’s
sunken eyes.

00:06:48.479 --> 00:06:53.900
So, instead it began to gravitate towards
the shadowy confines of the caves, not unlike

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:58.360
the usual darkness of its containment chamber
back at the Foundation.

00:06:58.360 --> 00:07:03.960
Traversing through long, winding corridors
of stone, SCP-096 found itself having to bend

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:09.100
down, to avoid hitting its head on the cave’s
low ceiling – obviously, this formation

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:13.069
of rocky blocks hadn’t formed with someone
of the Shy Guy’s height in mind.

00:07:13.069 --> 00:07:17.389
There was a low, warm glow coming from the
farthest side of the tunnel, and the thin

00:07:17.389 --> 00:07:22.840
creature made its way closer and closer, despite
the stone walls around it feeling like a tighter

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:24.910
confinement than its cell.

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:30.099
Approaching the source of the light, SCP-096
was relieved that the cave opened out into

00:07:30.099 --> 00:07:35.220
a more spacious area, the cramped tunnel giving
way to an expansive chamber that lay within

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:37.090
the heart of the mountain.

00:07:37.090 --> 00:07:42.280
The warm, orangey glow had been coming from
a flowing stream of boiling hot lava, that

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:46.860
seemed to trickle down from somewhere above,
creating a deadly, fiery pool directly in

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:48.120
the Shy Guy’s path.

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:53.930
But just before it could turn back and leave
the cave through the way he came, SCP-096

00:07:53.930 --> 00:07:58.120
sensed that familiar feeling of something
observing him.

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:02.370
Across the lava pool, on the other side, was
a creature comprised of a green cube for a

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:06.840
head, with a long, armless cuboid body, and
four cubed feet.

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:10.861
If it had been present in the real world,
it might have been made out of leaves, like

00:08:10.861 --> 00:08:12.190
a living shrub.

00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:16.730
It was staring directly at the Shy Guy from
across the lava, only for this strange newcomer

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:18.750
to disappear a moment later.

00:08:18.750 --> 00:08:23.800
The Creeper hissed, before it realized that
SCP-096 had leaped up behind it to land a

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:24.830
fatal blow.

00:08:24.830 --> 00:08:30.759
But little did the infamously anxious anomaly
realize the sentient shrub wasn’t done.

00:08:30.759 --> 00:08:36.849
There was a colossal boom that caused SCP-096
to stagger backwards, whimpering at the sudden

00:08:36.849 --> 00:08:40.310
loud explosion and the pain that had accompanied
it.

00:08:40.310 --> 00:08:45.580
The Creeper had blown itself to pieces, but
in doing so, had left a lasting injury, that

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:51.540
caused SCP-096 considerable discomfort as
it began limping towards the cave that led

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:54.310
out the opposite side of the mountain.

00:08:54.310 --> 00:08:58.580
Despite its injury, the Shy Guy was still
able to move with relative ease, and the further

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:01.670
it went, the more it seemed to gradually heal.

00:09:01.670 --> 00:09:06.329
However, it was as it stepped out once more
into the sunlight that the creature realized

00:09:06.329 --> 00:09:08.480
just how hungry it was.

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:12.750
Back in the real world, it hadn’t eaten
for several hours, and surprisingly – even

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:17.070
while accidentally stuck in digitized form
– the hunger mechanics of Minecraft were

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:20.730
having an effect on SCP-096.

00:09:20.730 --> 00:09:25.210
The Shy Guy started searching around for anything
that could prove to satiate its hunger.

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:31.019
There was a grove of trees not far, so SCP-096
lumbered closer to take a closer look.

00:09:31.019 --> 00:09:34.800
It couldn’t be certain, but it felt there
was at least a slim chance that there were

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:37.269
apples growing among the leaves.

00:09:37.269 --> 00:09:41.860
But even at the anomaly’s own elongated
height, it couldn’t simply reach up to pick

00:09:41.860 --> 00:09:42.860
them.

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:46.610
However, it was while swiping its arms up
at the tree that the Shy Guy swung its fist

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:48.420
and knocked the tree trunk.

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:53.050
To the creature’s surprise, it was able
to chip away at the wood with its hands, punching

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:57.200
at the tree until the trunk had been reduced
to a collection of wooden blocks that the

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:59.510
Shy Guy was able to collect.

00:09:59.510 --> 00:10:04.310
And sure enough, some red apples dropped from
the leaves above, enough to quell the hunger

00:10:04.310 --> 00:10:08.660
that SCP-096 was feeling, at least for the
time being.

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:10.750
Nearby, something was moving through the trees.

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:16.870
It was yet to lock eyes on SCP-096, but the
second it did, the mob would surely have sealed

00:10:16.870 --> 00:10:18.100
its own fate.

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:22.100
As it moved around, minding its own business,
the tall figure overheard the sounds of the

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:26.990
Shy Guy eating, and its attention was drawn
to where the creature was standing, enjoying

00:10:26.990 --> 00:10:28.160
an apple.

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:32.649
Sensing it had been seen, SCP-096 turned and
locked eyes with the entity.

00:10:32.649 --> 00:10:37.589
It was perhaps the only other being in Minecraft
that was a similar height and stature to the

00:10:37.589 --> 00:10:42.070
anomaly itself – in fact, the pair were
strikingly similar.

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:47.380
Before SCP-096 could carry out its usual method
of attack, the Enderman suddenly teleported

00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:48.440
out of view.

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:53.450
But it was too late now, both it and the Shy
Guy had looked at the other’s face; both

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:58.570
had been provoked, and were compelled to react
in exactly the same way.

00:10:58.570 --> 00:11:03.900
Just as SCP-096 entered its rage state, the
Enderman too opened its mouth and began to

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:09.660
shake, making loud, lengthy sounds not dissimilar
to the Shy Guy’s own angered screams.

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:12.140
But something profoundly strange happened
next.

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:18.089
SCP-096 and the Enderman kept attempting to
pursue one another, appearing in a new location

00:11:18.089 --> 00:11:22.139
within the Minecraft world, neither one getting
close enough to the other.

00:11:22.139 --> 00:11:26.420
They’d teleport, only for the other to teleport
away the moment they saw each other, each

00:11:26.420 --> 00:11:30.709
trying to catch one another but always staying
one step ahead or behind.

00:11:30.709 --> 00:11:35.200
This rapid chase almost became a strange,
ongoing sort of teleporting dance between

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:37.470
SCP-096 and the Enderman.

00:11:37.470 --> 00:11:42.269
At first, the Shy Guy had been compelled to
attack the Enderman, like it was with any

00:11:42.269 --> 00:11:43.890
who looked directly at it.

00:11:43.890 --> 00:11:47.960
But as they appeared and disappeared from
place to place, the creature started to feel

00:11:47.960 --> 00:11:50.670
an odd kinship with this shadowy fellow.

00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:56.010
It was so used to being frightened and alone,
to its overwhelming feelings of insecurity

00:11:56.010 --> 00:12:00.990
and self-loathing, that the simplicity of
just traversing the open world – with a

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:06.680
creature very alike itself in many ways – it
had all come as a welcome change.

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:12.190
SCP-096 found it therapeutic even, and before
long, was following the Enderman not out of

00:12:12.190 --> 00:12:18.500
any intention to do it harm, but just to feel,
for a while, like it had a friend.

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:24.769
Just a little bit longer, SCP-096 thought,
welcoming the enjoyment it felt playing this

00:12:24.769 --> 00:12:27.130
game of Minecraft.

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:32.850
Now go and check out “SCP-1471 MALO, BUT
HACKED MINECRAFT” and “SCP MINECRAFT WORLD

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:36.579
DESTROYER SCP-4335 - A WELT IN THE CRUCIBLE”
for more!

